E1 set-independent: YES (=13/7=1.857)
E2 (pair) argmax: Sidon/lacunary -- NOT the AP => pair level cannot detect AP
E3 (triple) argmax: AP {1..13} -- the AP => AP-extremality is 3rd-order

PROVABLE CONSEQUENCE: E1(AP)=E1(cov) and E2(AP)<E2(Sidon), so a lower bound on L from
(E1,E2) alone cannot exceed L(AP)=0 => gives only L(cov)>=0 (trivial). The covering-min
proof MUST use E3 (triple/SL(3)) -- the three-distance/Freiman inverse, non-local, 3rd-order.
This EXPLAINS the failure of union bound, 2nd moment, Chebyshev, Paley-Zygmund, deg-2 dual.
